BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Soul Patrol
DTSTART:20260511T230000Z
DTEND:20260512T005500Z
DTSTAMP:20260511T230000Z
UID:7t7371TkDN
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 98 mins (1h38m)\n\nThe Vietnam War's first all-Black
  special operations team spent decades in silence. Now\, fifty years later
 \, they gather one last time to tell the story America forgot to tell.Dire
 ctor J.M. Harper scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/sou
 l-patrol\n\nEstimated start: 16:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Again Again
DTSTART:20260512T013000Z
DTEND:20260512T032500Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T013000Z
UID:OOtO7YykAJ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nAberdeen-raised director Mia Moor
 e’s debut film\, executive produced by Lilly Wachowski\, is a heady\, ro
 mantic sci-fi starring a trans woman who enters a new day after ten years 
 stuck in “the loop.”Director Mia Moore\, Producer Cliff Noonan\, and E
 xecutive Producer Ian Schrank scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net
 /festival/again-again\n\nEstimated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Barbara Forever
DTSTART:20260512T040000Z
DTEND:20260512T060000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040000Z
UID:nYxZ4edb4H
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nFor five decades\, avant-garde f
 eminist filmmaker Barbara Hammer created groundbreaking lesbian cinema—e
 xploring identity\, gender\, and sexuality\, uncovering erased histories\,
  and putting lesbian lives boldly\, joyfully\, and unapologetically on scr
 een.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/barbara-forever\n\nEstimated start: 
 21:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lucky Lu
DTSTART:20260512T193000Z
DTEND:20260512T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T193000Z
UID:odb5LYLUA0
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 103 mins (1h43m)\n\nA NYC delivery rider’s world i
 s turned upside down when he loses his only source of income. With his fam
 ily on their way from Asia\, Lu is forced to navigate the unforgiving city
  and fight to protect the fragile life he’s spent years building.\n\nhtt
 ps://www.siff.net/festival/lucky-lu\n\nEstimated start: 12:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
